.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt PTS 4
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pts
.Nd pseudo-terminal driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In stdlib.h
.Ft int
.Fn posix_openpt "int oflag"
.In pty.h
.Ft int
.Fn openpty "int *master" "int *slave" "char *name" "const struct termios *termp" "const struct winsize *winp"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A pseudo-terminal is a pair of character devices: a master, held by a
program such as a terminal emulator,
.Xr script 1
or
.Xr sudo 8 ,
and a slave,
.Pa /dev/pts/ Ns Ar N ,
on which another program runs as on any terminal.
Output written to the slave, after its output processing, is read from the
master; data written to the master is the slave's input, edited and echoed
by its line discipline as keyboard input is.
.Pp
Each open of
.Pa /dev/ptmx
creates a pair and returns its master.
The slave's number
.Ar N
is the lowest one free, and
.Xr ptsname 3
gives its name.
Its node is created owned by the opener's real user ID, mode 0600, and
can't be opened until
.Xr unlockpt 3 ;
.Xr grantpt 3
has nothing to do.
.Xr openpty 3
does all of this.
.Pp
Closing the master hangs up the slave: the session it controls gets
.Dv SIGHUP ,
reads of the slave return end-of-file and writes fail with
.Er EIO .
Once every slave descriptor is closed, reads of the master return
end-of-file.
The pair and its node go away when both sides are closed.
.Pp
On the master,
.Dv TCGETS ,
.Dv TCSETS
and
.Dv TIOCSWINSZ
and their companions act on the slave, and these requests are
supported:
.Bl -tag -width TIOCSPTLCK
.It Dv TIOCGPTN
Store the slave's number.
.It Dv TIOCSPTLCK
Lock (nonzero) or unlock (zero) the slave.
.It Dv TIOCSIG
Send the signal given as the argument to the slave's foreground process
group.
.It Dv TIOCPKT
Turn packet mode on (nonzero) or off.
In packet mode each read returns either a zero byte followed by data, or a
single byte of
.Dv TIOCPKT_FLUSHREAD ,
.Dv TIOCPKT_FLUSHWRITE ,
.Dv TIOCPKT_STOP ,
.Dv TIOCPKT_START ,
.Dv TIOCPKT_NOSTOP
and
.Dv TIOCPKT_DOSTOP
bits saying what happened to the slave since the last read.
.El
.Pp
At most
.Va kern.tty.pty_max
pairs exist at once (256 by default); beyond that, opening
.Pa /dev/ptmx
fails with
.Er EAGAIN .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/pts/N -compact
.It Pa /dev/ptmx
creates pairs
.It Pa /dev/pts/ Ns Ar N
slaves
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openpty 3 ,
.Xr posix_openpt 3 ,
.Xr ptsname 3 ,
.Xr unlockpt 3 ,
.Xr termios 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
Pseudo-terminals appeared in
.Bx 4.2 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD; its device names are those of
.Nx
and
.Fx .
